{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/pulls/1","id":4863204326,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU6DMss8AAAABId6b5g","html_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/issues/1","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Avoid initializing disabled allocator events before a recorder exists","user":{"login":"codexcoder21","id":216437543,"node_id":"U_kgDODOaTJw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216437543?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21","html_url":"https://github.com/codexcoder21","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codexcoder21/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The owner asked for `testGracefulCloseEmitsSingleDisconnectedEvent` and `testConnectionListenerIsolation` to be fixed without widening their 2000 ms budgets after https://buildtest.kotlin.build/run?id=b5c6d8a2 blocked https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/pull/692 twice. Cold-dial measurements in https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/tree/fix/lane63-graceful-close-dial/investigation/lane63 and https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlResolver/pull/1262 led to this investigation of the first connection's setup cost.\n\nThe first multistream write calls the adaptive allocator's disabled JFR event checks. Each check first initializes an event singleton, registering event metadata even when no recorder exists. In counterbalanced fresh 128 MiB SerialGC JVMs, first-header writes had a median of 558 ms with that metadata cold, versus 92 ms when only the JFR runtime had already been initialized. Noise arithmetic was a smaller part of the dial. Preparing JFR alone did not eliminate every deadline failure, so it was retained as a diagnostic control, not adopted as a fix.\n\nThe adaptive and pooled allocators now leave event classes untouched until a recorder exists. The existing platform-capability check remains unchanged, and the enabled-state check still runs on every eligible operation. Allocation events enabled by name after earlier buffer use remain observable. Compile-only JFR stubs mirror the added JDK calls.\n\nA fresh-JVM test allocates, resizes and releases real heap and direct buffers, then checks the public event registry. Against the exact consumer dependency, Netty 4.2.10, this test failed 10/10 before the five adaptive guards and passed 10/10 afterward. The late-recording case also passed. Four regression cases are added to the existing JFR suite, with its existing Java 17 and timeout conditions unchanged.\n\nValidation:\n- Netty reactor source/style/test compilation passed on the final source; the four new cases passed in actual branch classes, with no skipped tests.\n- Both unchanged original UrlProtocol scenarios passed 10/10 fresh JVMs with the exact-version private patch. Current lane baselines were graceful 1/10 failures in the packed full-main jar (2/10 loose classes), listener 0/10; lane63's historical 10/10 and 8/10 failure batches remain separately identified.\n- Expanded existing JFR neighbour selection passed 7/8. `adaptiveJfrBufferAllocationThreadLocal` failed on `chunkThreadLocal=false`, full trace in the evidence branch. The same failure reproduced with unmodified origin/4.2 adaptive and pooled allocator classes (3/4 selected existing cases passed). Concurrent methods observe shared event names; producer scoping is a lead, not a completed fix. This draft is held for that failure and full CI; it is not presented as a clean expanded suite. All three unchanged UrlProtocol neighbours also passed: provider contract, outbound admission permit release, registered RPC binding replacement. Remote CI and full suites are frozen for this effort. No timeout, iteration count, assertion or production dependency version was changed, and nothing was published.\n\nParent handoff: url://handoff/handoffs/hf-2026-10-13-restore-tinysite-publishing-diagnose-the-tinysite-to-filedrop-relay-forward-failed-outage-decide-the-urlresolver-pr-1226-design-land-the-outage-fix-prs-and-redeploy-sfs-filedrop-tinysite . Evidence: https://github.com/CodexCoder21Organization/UrlProtocol/tree/fix/lane88-cold-first-dial/investigation/lane88 .\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","created_at":"2026-10-14T19:16:58Z","updated_at":"2026-10-14T19:19:18Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"95033e65a86942ae34dcea4bac58e907b94476fa","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/issues/1/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CodexCoder21Organization/netty/statuses/8094800230100d820c3215b51485b9f2e3db30b0","head":{"label":"CodexCoder21Organization:fix/lane88-defer-dis